'''Chiraneau''' was a [[human]] who served in the [[Imperial Navy|Navy]] of the [[Galactic Empire]] and worked as a [[Rear Admiral]] and an [[advisor]] to [[Fleet Admiral]] [[Firmus Piett]]. The Rear Admiral was a part of both the [[Imperial Navy's officer corps|Navy's officer corps]] and [[Imperial Starfighter Corps|starfighter corps]], [[pilot]]ing a [[VT-49 Decimator]]. In [[4 ABY]], Chiraneau was present on board the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station|Death Star II]] [[battle station]] and was among the [[Imperial officer]]s present when the [[Dark Lord of the Sith|Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] arrived on board.

==Biography==
[[File:Rear_Admiral_Chiraneau_TCGTFM.png|thumb|left|300px|Chiraneau served as a rear admiral in the Imperial Navy and as advisor to Admiral Firmus Piett.]]
Chiraneau was a [[human]] who served as a [[Rear Admiral]] in the [[Imperial Navy's officer corps|officer corps]] of the [[Imperial Navy]] of the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="X-Wing" /> They functioned as an [[advisor]] to<ref name="VT-49" /> [[Fleet Admiral]]<ref name="To the Last">{{StoryCite|story=To the Last|book=From a Certain Point of View: Return of the Jedi}}</ref> [[Firmus Piett]],<ref name="VT-49" /> the [[Commanding officer|commander]] of the [[Executor-class Star Dreadnought|''Executor''-class Star Dreadnought]] ''[[Executor]]'' and [[Death Squadron]].<ref name="USW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> Chiraneau also [[Imperial Starfighter Pilot|flew]] in the [[Imperial Starfighter Corps]].<ref name="VT-49" />

In [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of {{Film|VI}} to [[4 ABY]].</ref> Chiraneau was present on board the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station|Death Star II]] [[battle station]] while it was under construction in the [[Endor system]]. When the [[Dark Lord of the Sith|Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] arrived on the [[space station]] to inspect the progress of its construction, Chiraneau was among the group of [[Imperial officer]]s who stood silently at attention in one of the station's [[hangar]]s as Vader disembarked from his [[ST 321|shuttle]] and spoke with [[Moff]] [[Tiaan Jerjerrod]], [[commander]] of the [[Death Star]].<ref name="ROTJ" /> In the hope of showing Chiraneau and the others present how aligned and attuned he and Vader were based on the harmony in the choreography of their parting, Jerjerrod matched the [[Sith]]'s gait and rhythm when leaving the hangar.<ref name="ROTJ FACPOV">{{StoryCite|story=Any Work Worth Doing|book=From a Certain Point of View: Return of the Jedi}}</ref> Not long after Vader's arrival, the Death Star II was destroyed by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] during the [[Battle of Endor]].<ref name="ROTJ" />

==Personality and traits==
Chiraneau had light skin and [[Color|gray]] [[hair]].<ref name="ROTJ" />

==Equipment==
[[File:RearAdmiralChiraneauVT49Decimator-XWM.png|thumb|300px|Chiraneau piloted a VT-49 Decimator.]]
The Rear Admiral wore a gray [[Imperial officer's uniform]] including a matching [[Imperial kepi|cap]] with an [[officer's disk]] and a black [[belt]] that also bore an [[officer]]'s disk on its buckle. Chiraneau also wore black [[boot]]s and black [[glove]]s<ref name="ROTJ" /> and bore a [[rank insignia plaque]] with six red pips above six blue pips. They owned at least two [[code cylinder]]s<ref name="X-Wing" /> and [[pilot]]ed a [[VT-49 Decimator]].<ref name="VT-49" />

==Behind the scenes==
Chiraneau first appeared in the [[original trilogy]] film [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']],<ref name="ROTJ" /> which was released on [[March 25]], [[1983]].<ref name="YbY">''[[Star Wars Year By Year: A Visual History, New Edition]]''</ref> [[Mike Havord]] portrayed the character<ref name="EastBristol">{{WebCite|url=https://bid.eastbristol.co.uk/past-auctions/sreas10560/lot-details/8657729d-8fb5-4d99-b26a-ae2a01070019|text=Star Wars - Imperial Officers - Autograph Collection|work=[https://eastbristol.co.uk/ East Bristol Auctions]|archivedate=20240814145604}}</ref> as well as<ref name="CelebrityInk">{{WebCite|url=https://celebrityinkautographs.co.uk/products/mike-havord-as-colonel-jendon-star-wars|text=MIKE HAVORD as Colonel Jendon - Star Wars|work=[http://celebrityinkautographs.co.uk Celebrity Ink Autographs]|archivedate=20240712103611}}</ref> [[Colonel]] [[Jendon]] in the film.<ref name="AMG">{{AtomicMassGames|url=transmission/star-wars-x-wing-battle-over-endor-imperial-preview|text=Star Wars: X-Wing &mdash; Battle Over Endor Imperial Preview}}</ref> According to<ref name="Facebook">[[:File:MikeHavord-KennethCoombsFacebook.png|Facebook message]] from [[Kenneth Coombs]] &mdash; Used with permission</ref> actor<ref name="Memorabilia">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-in-the-uk-memorabilia-23-24-november-2013|text=Star Wars in the UK: Memorabilia, 23-24 November 2013}}</ref> [[Kenneth Coombs]], Havord had also portrayed an Imperial officer in the [[1977]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']], although this character has not been identified as Chiraneau, Jendon, or a separate individual.<ref name="Facebook" /> The hangar scene was filmed on Stage 6 at [[Elstree Studios]] between [[February 22]] and [[February 24]], [[1982]]. The floor of the hangar had to be repainted several times due to the movement and positioning of the various extras on the set, which caused regular damage.<ref name="MakingOf">''[[The Making of Return of the Jedi]]''</ref> Production photos reveal that Chiraneau appeared in an additional scene made for ''Return of the Jedi'' that did not make the final cut of the film. In the scene, Chiraneau and several other Imperial officers accompany Vader as they approach the Death Star's hangar in order to greet [[Galactic Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] upon his arrival.<ref name="T-bone">{{WebCite|url=http://www.starwarz.com/tbone/index.php?categoryid=11&p2_articleid=5|text=T-bone's Star Wars Universe - Return of the Jedi - Off To See The Emperor|author=T-bone|date=2003-06-03|work=T-bone's Star Wars Universe|archivedate=20071112111838}}</ref>

[[File:VaderJerjerrodDeletedScene-SWITGGV.png|thumb|left|300px|Chiraneau in an additional deleted scene set as the Emperor arrived on the Death Star II]]
In the film, Chiraneau and all other officers in his scene are depicted with a rank insignia plaque showing three red squares above three blue,<ref name="ROTJ" /> which denotes a commander.<ref name="Hidalgo Tweet Rank plaques 2">{{Twitter|pablohidalgo|status/722602214594752513|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|quote=@StompinSteveB No, everyone's is wrong in ROTJ. It was EVERYONE IS A COMMANDER DAY at Endor.|nobackup=1}}</ref> However, on a card released in the [[2015]] ''[[Imperial Assault Carrier Expansion Pack]]'' made by [[Fantasy Flight Games]] for the ''[[Star Wars: X-Wing Miniatures Game]]'', which was also the first source to identify Chiraneau in [[canon]], the character is depicted with a plaque showing six red squares over six blue.<ref name="X-Wing" /> As the rank plaques shown in ''Return of the Jedi'' have been acknowledged to be a costuming error,<ref name="25 years">{{InsiderCite|105|25 Years of Return of the Jedi!|25 Years of ''Return of the Jedi''!}}</ref> this article treats the card to be correct.<ref name="X-Wing" />

Footage of Vader's arrival on the second Death Star was reused for his return from<ref name="ESB">{{Film|V}}</ref> the [[planet]]<ref name="USWNE">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> [[Bespin]] to<ref name="ESB" /> his [[flagship]], the ''Executor'',<ref name="USWNE" /> in the [[1997]] [[The Star Wars Trilogy Special Edition|''Special Edition'']] release of [[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back|''The Empire Strikes Back'']]. As such, Havord is seen in the ''Special Edition'' version alongside other extras who portrayed Imperial officers in ''Return of the Jedi'', however, this article assumes these to be separate characters.<ref name="ESB">{{Film|V}}</ref> Chiraneau's name originated in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, where it was first used on a card in the [[2000]] ''[[Death Star II Limited]]'' expansion set of the [[Star Wars Customizable Card Game|''Star Wars'' Customizable Card Game]] produced by [[Decipher]]<ref name="CCG">{{CCG|set=Death Star II Limited|cardname=Admiral Chiraneau}}</ref>

